mainmenu "The pico C ABI on the T2G kit: zenoh-pico's program over wz"

rsource "../zephyr-common/Kconfig.wz"
rsource "../zephyr-eth-wzmac/Kconfig.zeth"

# The program is the comparison image's (deploy/zephyr-pico-compare/src/main.c), which reads the
# router it connects to from this symbol; the default is that image's, so the two dial the same
# router.
config PICO_COMPARE_LOCATOR
	string "The router the node connects to"
	default "udp/192.168.100.1:7447"
	help
	  The program runs as a client of a router on the bench host, over UDP unicast, as the
	  comparison image does. The router listens on this locator. Empty, the program leaves
	  the open to scout for a router, as upstream's z_queryable.c does with an empty LOCATOR:
	  both images carry scouting (Z_FEATURE_SCOUTING), as zenoh-pico's default build does, and
	  this one scouts over one datagram socket of Zephyr's stack, as zenoh-pico does on Zephyr.

config WZ_PICO_ABI_MULTI_THREAD
	bool "zenoh-pico's multi-threaded arm (Z_FEATURE_MULTI_THREAD)"
	help
	  The header the program compiles against and the Rust half are both built for pico's
	  multi-threaded arm: the session's read task is a thread of the cooperative engine
	  (CONFIG_WZ_OS), started by the open, and `main` only declares and waits. Without it the
	  program steps the session itself (`zp_spin_once`). The two arms allocate different structs,
	  so the header and the library are always built for the same one.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
